  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "In a cave on San Cha Mountain, the Ten Tyrants gather and report that Hu Mei Er used them to test the black and white demons, with seventh and tenth brother injured. Tyrant Heng Mei slaps the second brother, says heavily injured is perfect as long as they are not dead, says this is San Cha mountain not Nan mountain, and warns that Kong Ri Tian, Long Qing Tian, Wu Shen Tong, and Yi Chong can kill them like ants, and that they stay here because of him. He forbids trouble with Hu Mei Er because of her ties to Lin San Chi, Li Xian, and Mo Wu Tian. He sighs that the three kings inheritance is no small matter and that rank four and five Gu Masters on the mountain are restraining each other. He then says the Ten Tyrants of Nan mountain cannot take this lying down and will visit the black and white demons personally. The brothers call him a senior of the demonic path who was roaming when the pair were still babies; he chides them, plans to mention working together against Hu Mei Er, and use the young pair as vanguard.",
      "chapters": [
        339
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_san_cha_mountain",
        "fac_ten_tyrants",
        "char_hu_mei_er",
        "loc_nan_mountain",
        "char_kong_ri_tian",
        "char_long_qing_tian",
        "char_wu_shen_tong",
        "char_yi_chong",
        "char_lin_san_chi",
        "char_li_xian",
        "char_mo_wu_tian",
        "fac_gu_masters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He has a robust body, a bare flat chest, and black chest hair growing all over his chest. When he wears a smile and cups his hands, at first glance he looks like an elegant black bear.",
      "chapters": [
        340
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Outside Fang Yuan’s cave he announces he came to pay a visit. Bai Ning Bing recalls he is boss of Ten Tyrants, cultivates strength path, likes to eat little children’s flesh, and has spread fear over Nanshan. Eight people stand outside; at the front is a robust figure with a bare flat chest and black chest hair, rank four middle stage aura, who commanded the other nine members of Ten Tyrants and lorded over Nan mountain for many years. Famous for savageness, he wears a smile, cups his hands, and at first glance looks like an elegant black bear. He speaks loudly on purpose and draws nearby Gu Masters’ attention.",
      "chapters": [
        340
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "visit-outside-the-cave",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "char_bai_ning_bing",
        "path_strength"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan challenges a life and death battle and attacks. Heng Mei activates violent strength Gu, his body enlarges, and he blocks head-on; after one exchange he judges himself stronger than Fang Yuan’s rank four initial stage, but he does not take the initiative because Bai Ning Bing is also there. Fang Yuan fights him while Bai Ning Bing suppresses the remaining members. Midway he grows fearful that Fang Yuan’s Gu worm combination is superior and that the youth fights like a hundred year old monster; his fighting spirit falls and he hesitates to strike. Bai Ning Bing kills the other members and locks him down as Fang Yuan’s six beast phantoms beat him to a pulp, with internal organs and bone fragments on the ground.",
      "chapters": [
        340
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "visit-outside-the-cave",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_violent_strength_gu",
        "sys_gu_worms"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Camp talk pairs the killing with Fei Li’s end and Fang Yuan’s challenge to Sky Tiger Xue San Si.",
      "chapters": [
        341
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "camp-talk-after-the-killing",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fei_li",
        "char_xue_san_si"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Later recount says he visited little beast king out of goodwill but was killed, and that little beast king used initial stage cultivation to kill rank four middle stage Gu Masters outright.",
      "chapters": [
        342
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "goodwill-recount",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
